{"id": "EUVD-2026-106906", "enisaUuid": "daa80599-7425-34c1-830d-12d385ea6d06", "description": "adm-zip 0.6.0 contains a decompression bomb protection bypass that allows attackers to evade the maxOutputLength guard by targeting the asynchronous getDataAsync() path in methods/inflater.js. Attackers can craft ZIP entries with falsified small declared sizes and high-ratio DEFLATE payloads to exhaust memory in applications reading entries asynchronously.", "datePublished": "2026-10-21T00:37:04", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T00:37:04", "baseScore": 6.9, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:N/VC:N/VI:N/VA:L/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/cthackers/adm-zip/security/advisories/GHSA-c6fg-446q-cg94", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/adm-zip-0.6.0-decompression-bomb-guard-bypass-via-getdataasync"], "aliases": ["GHSA-x5pg-q574-6h2m", "CVE-2026-114103"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.27, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "48f99e1c-3a99-3580-bcda-0cbe6811a5b6", "product": {"name": "adm-zip", "vendor": {"name": "Node.js"}}, "product_version": "0.6.0 <0.6.1"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "67515874-1679-38a6-9963-6e85f2dbedc4", "vendor": {"name": "cthackers"}}], "isExploited": false}